.TH "CSDLC-BIND" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-bind \- bind an issue to its registered execution checkout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc bind ISSUE
.fi
.nf
\&csdlc bind \-\-request REQUEST \-\-registry REGISTRY \-\-registrations REGISTRATIONS
\&  [\-\-repo\-root ROOT] [\-\-v3\-state\-root ROOT]
\&csdlc bind \-\-help
.fi
.SH ISSUE INTENT FORM
\&The #869 issue intent forms are a candidate contract, pending the required exact\-head validation/review and separate installation/activation. They do not replace the active operator binary. Existing \-\-request forms below retain their existing native contracts. See docs/csdlc\-v3/INTENT_COMMANDS.md for complete strict content and effect boundaries.
.PP
\&Bind the prepared issue through the existing registered\-worktree owner; derive registry and registration inputs from canonical context.
.PP
\&Optional \-\-repo\-root selects discovery, \-\-json retains machine output, and \-\-emit\-request returns a generated wrapper accepted directly by COMMAND \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json; its inner request is also accepted. Both forms share identity and mutation guards.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.PP
\&Requires ready issue\-specific cards, current digest, authenticated canonical authority and the tracked .adl/worktree\-policy.json approved parent. Creates the exact branch and FastWork checkout when absent, or validates supported existing binding. Do not manually create a competing checkout. Verify bound phase, returned digest and all six cards before implementation.
.SH EFFECTS
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.PP
\&Mutates Git branch/worktree and local issue state.
.PP
\&Do not interpret read_only in an older report as a byte\-level filesystem guarantee. See csdlc(1) for current observation guarantees, selected\-binary discovery and the primary/linked path distinction.
.SH OPTIONS
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.PP
\&\-\-request: Required path to a UTF\-8 JSON request of the command's request family.
.PP
\&\-\-registry: Required path to docs/templates/prompts/current.json; selects the active versioned templates and schemas.
.PP
\&\-\-registrations: Required JSON array of actual Git worktree registrations, each {branch, worktree, primary}; refresh from live git worktree list \-\-porcelain.
.PP
\&\-\-repo\-root: Explicit repository discovery root. Required by foundation/sprint; optional for local\-family commands. It does not override authenticated binding guards.
.PP
\&\-\-v3\-state\-root: Optional retained construction state root for issue/eligibility; not a primary\-checkout artifact location or an ownership bypass.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show standalone help; \-h is equivalent.
.PP
\&\-h: Show standalone help; do not combine with execution options.
.SH REQUEST
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.PP
\&LocalPreparationRequest; complete fields, commands and canonical locations are in csdlc\-requests(1). Example source: docs/csdlc\-v3/man/examples/local.json. Replace example identity with the actual issue, approved branch/worktree, active registry version and latest lifecycle digest before operational use.
.SH EXAMPLES
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.nf
\&csdlc bind \-\-request local\-request.json \e
\&  \-\-registry docs/templates/prompts/current.json \e
\&  \-\-registrations actual\-registrations.json
.fi
.PP
\&The checked\-in example is fixture\-validated. A JSON\-valid example does not grant an operational binding or assert dependency readiness. Use csdlc\-workflow(1) to prepare and refresh these inputs from real state.
.SH RECOVERY
\&The following details describe the retained request\-based form. The candidate issue intent form is specified above.
.PP
\&Preserve index, values and transaction bytes. Reissue the exact interrupted mutating issue/bind/edit request through its native owner after checking the bound topology; do not use diagnostics as a repair command. If current recovery is denied, retain the finding and route a bounded tooling repair. Never hand\-edit transaction stages/backups or stale digest guards.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1).
